    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0417" n="411" xml:id="pg411"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Stevens to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-03-01"><hi rendition="#italic">March 1,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>All quiet throughout archipelago. Protectorate is preventing pressure of the
                    British minister. The Japanese representatives telegraphed Government January
                    19. Japanese ship <hi rendition="#italic">Naniwa</hi> arrived February 23. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kongo</hi> arrived January 28. It is believed that the
                    Japanese representative who arrived November 28 is urged by the British
                    minister. It is believed that the British ship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Warspite</hi> has been ordered here to provide for contingencies. It is
                    advisable to send here at once the most powerful American ship available. I have
                    sent particulars by mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
